Based on our discussion with David Kempfer and Jennie Coffey during the 7/21/2026 meeting, the scope for this user story has been updated as follows:
Toggle Configuration: Administrative pre-approval is a single standalone toggle. This is not tied to any individual authorization/function code. A designee may hold multiple admin function codes, but there's one on/off switch covering "administrative" as a category.
Access Control: Managing Specialist role only. Confirmed via a live demo: the Management Information Links tab shows only 3 links under the ASI role, versus the full set (including approvals) under the MS role. this toggle follows that same existing role restriction.
Automation Behavior: Fully automatic and final. Once submitted, the system approves it and no manual review or reject step remains for that request.
Default State: Unchecked by default. For both newly appointed designees and existing designees already in the system. No retroactive "turn on" behavior. 
